fcitx5-marathi-transliterate (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Many more words can be typed, and ambiguous typing now offers every real
    reading: doubled letters, ज्ञ, ृ/ऋ, ऱ्य, ः, ॅ/ॉ, ठ्ठ and ं, including ं
    with no nasal typed.
  * z and f now give झ and फ; long words are no longer given up on.
  * Bug fix: pressing Space no longer loses the word in Chromium-based
    browsers.
  * The candidate popup is now a fixed-size, compact, rounded list showing
    five words, which scrolls instead of paging.

 -- Maatra maintainers <nobody@localhost>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0530

fcitx5-marathi-transliterate (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bug fix: Tab no longer leaks through to the application while composing
    a word, which previously moved keyboard focus out of the text field
    instead of just being ignored. Tab / Shift+Tab now cycle the candidate
    popup highlight, matching Fcitx5's own default bindings and Down/Up.
  * Bug fix: the inline preedit text now follows the highlighted candidate
    when it is moved with Up/Down/Tab/Shift+Tab, instead of always showing
    the top candidate regardless of what was highlighted.

 -- Maatra maintainers <nobody@localhost>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 23:02:51 +0530

